{
  "name": "Exercise sEt 4.2",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "9-math-3-ex4.2-q1",
      "questionNumber": 1,
      "question": "Factor completely: **(i)** $9x^2 + 24xy + 16y^2$ **(ii)** $4s^2 + 20st + 25t^2$ **(iii)** $49x^2 + 28xy + 4y^2$ **(iv)** $64p^2 + \\frac{32}{3}pq + \\frac{4}{9}q^2$ **(v)** $3a^2 + 4ab + \\frac{4}{3}b^2$ **(vi)** $\\frac{9}{5}s^2 + 6sv + 5v^2$",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**Recall the identity:** $a^2 + 2ab + b^2 = (a + b)^2$. We match each expression with this form."
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**(i) $9x^2 + 24xy + 16y^2$:** $9x^2 = (3x)^2$, $16y^2 = (4y)^2$, and $24xy = 2(3x)(4y)$. So: $$9x^2 + 24xy + 16y^2 = (3x + 4y)^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**(ii) $4s^2 + 20st + 25t^2$:** $4s^2 = (2s)^2$, $25t^2 = (5t)^2$, and $20st = 2(2s)(5t)$. So: $$4s^2 + 20st + 25t^2 = (2s + 5t)^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 4,
          "content": "**(iii) $49x^2 + 28xy + 4y^2$:** $49x^2 = (7x)^2$, $4y^2 = (2y)^2$, and $28xy = 2(7x)(2y)$. So: $$49x^2 + 28xy + 4y^2 = (7x + 2y)^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 5,
          "content": "**(iv) $64p^2 + \\frac{32}{3}pq + \\frac{4}{9}q^2$:** $64p^2 = (8p)^2$, $\\frac{4}{9}q^2 = \\left(\\frac{2}{3}q\\right)^2$, and $2(8p)\\left(\\frac{2}{3}q\\right) = \\frac{32}{3}pq$. So: $$64p^2 + \\frac{32}{3}pq + \\frac{4}{9}q^2 = \\left(8p + \\frac{2}{3}q\\right)^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 6,
          "content": "**(v) $3a^2 + 4ab + \\frac{4}{3}b^2$:** Take out the common factor 3: $$3\\left(a^2 + \\frac{4}{3}ab + \\frac{4}{9}b^2\\right) = 3\\left(a + \\frac{2}{3}b\\right)^2$$ since $a^2 = (a)^2$, $\\frac{4}{9}b^2 = \\left(\\frac{2}{3}b\\right)^2$ and $2(a)\\left(\\frac{2}{3}b\\right) = \\frac{4}{3}ab$."
        },
        {
          "step": 7,
          "content": "**(vi) $\\frac{9}{5}s^2 + 6sv + 5v^2$:** Take out the common factor $\\frac{1}{5}$: $$\\frac{1}{5}(9s^2 + 30sv + 25v^2) = \\frac{1}{5}(3s + 5v)^2$$ since $9s^2 = (3s)^2$, $25v^2 = (5v)^2$ and $2(3s)(5v) = 30sv$."
        }
      ],
      "answer": "(i) (3x + 4y)²  (ii) (2s + 5t)²  (iii) (7x + 2y)²  (iv) (8p + 2/3 q)²  (v) 3(a + 2/3 b)²  (vi) (1/5)(3s + 5v)²",
      "verified": true,
      "formulaBox": {
        "title": "Perfect Square Trinomial",
        "content": "$$a^2 + 2ab + b^2 = (a + b)^2$$"
      },
      "notes": "**Exam Tip:** In parts (v) and (vi), first take out a common factor so that the remaining expression is a perfect square trinomial."
    },
    {
      "id": "9-math-3-ex4.2-q2",
      "questionNumber": 2,
      "question": "Find the values of the following using the identity $(a - b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2$: **(i)** $(79)^2$ **(ii)** $(193)^2$ **(iii)** $(299)^2$",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**(i) $(79)^2$:** Write $79 = 80 - 1$. $$(80 - 1)^2 = 80^2 - 2 \\times 80 \\times 1 + 1^2 = 6400 - 160 + 1 = 6241$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**(ii) $(193)^2$:** Write $193 = 200 - 7$. $$(200 - 7)^2 = 200^2 - 2 \\times 200 \\times 7 + 7^2 = 40000 - 2800 + 49 = 37249$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**(iii) $(299)^2$:** Write $299 = 300 - 1$. $$(300 - 1)^2 = 300^2 - 2 \\times 300 \\times 1 + 1^2 = 90000 - 600 + 1 = 89401$$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "(i) 6241  (ii) 37249  (iii) 89401",
      "verified": true,
      "formulaBox": {
        "title": "Square of a Difference",
        "content": "$$(a - b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2$$"
      },
      "notes": "**Exam Tip:** Use (a − b)² when the number is just below a round number (like 79 = 80 − 1)."
    }
  ]
}
